===Morocco vs Iran===
[[File:2018 FIFA World Cup Group B march IRN-MAR 25.jpg|thumb|[[Mbark Boussoufa]] vs [[Rouzbeh Cheshmi]]]]
The two teams had never met before.<ref name=Kit>{{cite web|url=https://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180508111620/http://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |url-status=dead |archive-date=8 May 2018 |title=2018 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit|website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association}}</ref>

[[Amine Harit]] fired wide with a volley from the edge of the penalty area after two minutes. [[Younès Belhanda]] and [[Medhi Benatia]] squandered close-range chances in a penalty box before Iran finally countered after 20 minutes, only for [[Karim Ansarifard]] to scuff his shot when clean through on goal. [[Sardar Azmoun]] then latched onto [[Omid Ebrahimi]]'s through ball, but his shot was too low and [[Munir Mohand Mohamedi|Munir Mohamedi]] saved low with his feet.<ref name="Goal-Morocco v Iran">{{cite web |last=Creek |first=Stephen |title=Bouhaddouz own-goal gifts game to Queiroz's men |url=http://www.goal.com/en/news/8/main/2018/06/15/45550852/morocco-0-iran-1-bouhaddouz-own-goal-gifts-game-to-queirozs |website=Goal.com |date=15 June 2018}}</ref> In the final 10 minutes [[Hakim Ziyech]] lashed the ball towards the bottom-left corner of the net from 20 yards but [[Alireza Beiranvand]] stopped the ball. In the last minutes, [[Ehsan Hajsafi]]'s delivery from the left was met by a header from [[Aziz Bouhaddouz]] that flew into the left corner of his own net.<ref name="Goal-Morocco v Iran"/><ref name="BBC 0-1">{{cite web |last=Emons |first=Michael |title=Morocco 0 Iran 1 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44408322 |work=BBC Sport |date=15 June 2018}}</ref><ref name="MAR-IRN recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/iran-snatch-late-win-with-own-goal-heartbreak |title=Own goal hands Iran dramatic victory |publisher=FIFA |date=15 June 2018 |access-date=15 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520043029/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/iran-snatch-late-win-with-own-goal-heartbreak |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

Iran won just their second match at the World Cup (D3 L8), with this is their first victory since beating the United States [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group F#United States vs Iran|2–1]] in [[1998 FIFA World Cup|June 1998]]. Iran did not attempt a single shot in the second half and were the first team since [[1966 FIFA World Cup|1966]] to score a goal in a half of World Cup football without attempting a shot.<ref name="Goal-Morocco v Iran"/><ref name="BBC 0-1"/> Iran also maintained their unbeaten streak against [[Confederation of African Football|CAF]] teams in the World Cup, having drawn [[Angola national football team|Angola]] 1–1 in 2006 and [[Nigeria national football team|Nigeria]] 0–0 in 2014; while this was also Iran's first ever victory against any Arab team in the World Cup.
