===Portugal vs Spain===
[[File:Portugal Spain 2018-06-15 02.jpg|thumb|Portugal vs Spain]]
{{see also|Portugal–Spain football rivalry}}
The two teams had met in 35 previous matches, including in the round of 16 of the [[2010 FIFA World Cup]], won by Spain [[2010 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Spain vs Portugal|1–0]]. Their most recent meeting was in the [[UEFA Euro 2012]] semi-finals, when Spain won 4–2 on penalties after a goalless draw in normal time.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180508111620/http://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |url-status=dead |archive-date=8 May 2018 |title=2018 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |page=6}}</ref>

[[Cristiano Ronaldo]] scored with an early penalty, winning it after he was fouled by [[Nacho (footballer, born 1990)|Nacho]] inside the box.<ref name="POR-ESP recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/156-por-esp-match-report-x-x-2957787 |title=Ronaldo illuminates stellar draw with Spain |publisher=FIFA |date=15 June 2018 |access-date=15 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520043225/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/156-por-esp-match-report-x-x-2957787 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> [[Diego Costa]] then twisted and turned away from two Portugal defenders to score with a low shot to the left corner which brought the two sides level.<ref name="Goal Portugal v Spain">{{cite web |last=Smith |first=Jamie |title=Brilliant Ronaldo hat-trick earns thrilling draw |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/portugal-v-spain/ca5gvudcr66pasfhzalrq0bmx |website=Goal.com |date=15 June 2018}}</ref> But just before the break, [[David de Gea]] fumbled a Ronaldo shot from outside the penalty box through his gloves and over the line.<ref name="BBC Portugal v Spain">{{cite web |last=Jennings |first=Patrick |title=Portugal 3 Spain 3 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44408323 |work=BBC Sport |date=15 June 2018}}</ref> Costa scored his second equaliser of the night just after the restart from close range before Nacho scored with a right foot half-volley in off the post from the edge of the penalty box, his first goal for Spain. As the clock ticked down, however, [[Gerard Piqué]] brought down Ronaldo just outside the box, with the Portugal star completing the scoring and his hat-trick with a free-kick into the top right corner of the net.<ref name="POR-ESP recap"/>

Ronaldo became the fourth player to score in four different World Cup tournaments ([[2006 FIFA World Cup|2006]], [[2010 FIFA World Cup|2010]], [[2014 FIFA World Cup|2014]] and [[2018 FIFA World Cup|2018]]) after [[Pelé]], [[Uwe Seeler]] and [[Miroslav Klose]], and also the first to score in eight consecutive World Cups and [[UEFA European Championship|European Championships]]. At age 33, Ronaldo also became the oldest hat-trick scorer in the World Cup, surpassing [[Rob Rensenbrink]] of the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]], who [[1978 FIFA World Cup Group 4#Netherlands vs Iran|scored three times against Iran]] in [[1978 FIFA World Cup|1978]], aged 30.<ref name="Goal Portugal v Spain"/><ref name="BBC Portugal v Spain"/> With this result, Spain has not won any opening matches since 2006, having lost to Switzerland 0–1 in 2010 and the Netherlands 1–5 in 2014.

