===Iran vs Portugal===
[[File:Iran and Portugal match at the FIFA World Cup 2018 3.jpg|thumb|[[Cristiano Ronaldo]] vs [[Saeid Ezatolahi]]]]
The two teams had met twice, most recently in a group stage game in the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]], won by Portugal [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group D#Portugal vs Iran|2–0]].<ref name=Kit5/>

In the 45 minute, [[Ricardo Quaresma]] cut in from the right before scoring with a curling shot off the outside of his right foot that looped over [[Alireza Beiranvand]] into the top-left corner. [[Saeid Ezatolahi]]'s foul on [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] won Portugal a penalty, which Ronaldo shot low into the right, enabling Beiranvand to get down and make a stop. Iran then managed to get a penalty in stoppage time after referee used VAR to determine that [[Cédric Soares|Cédric]]'s handball from [[Sardar Azmoun]]'s header had been intentional, which [[Karim Ansarifard]] converted high to his right. The game ended in a 1−1 draw, with Portugal advancing and Iran eliminated.<ref>{{cite web |last=Walker |first=Shaun |title=Iran close to stunning Portugal but Quaresma goal is enough |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2018/jun/25/iran-portugal-world-cup-group-b-match-report |publisher=The Guardian |date=25 June 2018}}</ref><ref name="IRN-POR recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/portugal-survives-with-dramatic-draw-375 |title=Portugal survive with dramatic draw |publisher=FIFA |date=25 June 2018 |access-date=25 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520051525/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/portugal-survives-with-dramatic-draw-375 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Ridge |first=Patric |title=Santos' men survive late Saransk scare after Ronaldo penalty miss |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/iran-v-portugal/16yubsgw1ht8bntdi6xyvf8q1 |website=Goal.com |date=25 June 2018}}</ref>

Quaresma (34 years, 272 days old) is the oldest player to score on his first World Cup start since [[Yahya Golmohammadi]] (35 years, 84 days old), who did so for Iran in 2006 [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group D#Mexico vs Iran|against Mexico]]. Iran's goal - scored after 92 minutes and 48 seconds - was the latest goal Portugal have ever conceded at the World Cup. This was Iran's best performance ever in the FIFA World Cup, winning four points and having earned their first ever draw against any European opponents since 1978, when Iran drew [[1978 FIFA World Cup Group 4#Scotland vs Iran|1–1]] to Scotland.<ref>{{cite web |last=Henry |first=Matthew |title=Iran 1 Portugal 1 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439228 |work=BBC Sport |date=25 June 2018}}</ref>

