===Spain vs Morocco===
[[File:Spain vs Morocco (14).jpg|thumb|[[Nordin Amrabat]] and [[Sergio Ramos]]]]
Despite their geographical proximity, the two teams had faced each other only in two opportunities, both were in the [[1962 FIFA World Cup]] qualification phase and [[1962 FIFA World Cup qualification (CAF–UEFA play-off)|won by Spain]].<ref name=Kit5/>

In the 14th minute, a mix-up between [[Sergio Ramos]] and [[Andrés Iniesta]] allowed [[Khalid Boutaïb]] to steal possession on the halfway line, burst through on goal and finish through the legs of [[David de Gea]]. Iniesta and [[Diego Costa]] combined to set up [[Isco]] for a close-range finish that tied the scores five minutes later. Boutaïb was clear again in the 25th minute when Morocco took a quick throw-in, but De Gea stopped the ball. [[Nordin Amrabat]], [[Manuel da Costa (footballer, born 1986)|Manuel da Costa]] and [[Mbark Boussoufa]] were all booked in three-minute period before [[Sergio Busquets]] headed over the crossbar from Isco's corner. Amrabat's strike from at least 25 yards out bounced off the woodwork in the 55th minute. Isco's looping header dipped under the crossbar, but [[Romain Saïss]] made a clearance, [[Gerard Piqué]] heading wide from the resulting Isco corner. [[Youssef En-Nesyri]] scored home a header to give Morocco the lead. And when [[Iago Aspas]] turned home [[Dani Carvajal]]'s cross from the right after a short corner – the goal given by VAR after a long delay – Spain was tied in the first minute of added time.<ref name="ESP-MAR recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/review-spain-morocco-591w-2968948 |title=Spain top group after thrilling finale |publisher=FIFA |date=25 June 2018 |access-date=25 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520051657/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/review-spain-morocco-591w-2968948 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Smith |first=Jamie |title=Spain tops group despite dramatic draw |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/spain-v-morocco/2aou8pglvyowf0si1thozthih |website=Goal.com |date=25 June 2018}}</ref>

Boutaïb's goal for Morocco was their first goal at the finals since 1998, when [[Salaheddine Bassir]] scored in a [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group A#Scotland vs Morocco|3–0]] win over Scotland. Ramos made his 16th appearance for Spain at the World Cup, overtaking [[Xavi (footballer, born 1980)|Xavi]] as their most capped outfield player in the competition. Spain have failed to win their final group game at a World Cup for the first time since 1982, having won the previous eight such games.<ref>{{cite web |last=Whalley |first=Mike |title=Spain 2 Morocco 2 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439235 |work=BBC Sport |date=25 June 2018}}</ref>

